  "kind": "fix",
  "title": "Bug fix for Brett.",
  "asked": "Bug fix for Brett. Read CLAUDE.md + _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md first. Finished headless builds never close their tmux session: deploy/claude-headless.sh waits for Enter (up to a day) after `claude -p` ends, so 35 finished `axf-*` sessions piled up and the agent cap / build queue counted them as busy and stopped starting new builds. Fix: 1. In deploy/claude-headless.sh: when run headless (no attached client) close the tmux session ~2 minutes after `claude -p` exits (keep the log files), instead of waiting a day. If someone is attached, keep the old wait-for-Enter. 2. Wherever the agent cap / queue counts running builds (the agent-cap build's code, find it with grep for the queue and max agents), count only live `claude -p` processes, never finished sessions. 3. Run the local test block + lifecycle check, then `git push origin HEAD:main` (merge origin/main first; notes files keep both sides). Short report at the end: thing touched, what was wrong, what changed. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once.",
